---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const REPO = 'https://github.com/hareeshagunasekara/iconnook';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What IconNook collects (almost nothing), what stays in your browser, and how to reach us."
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="section-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-text-muted">Last updated: 8 November 2026</p>
    <p class="mt-6 text-lg">
      IconNook is built to work without knowing who you are. There are no accounts, no sign-up, no
      ads and no tracking cookies.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">What stays in your browser</h2>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
      <li>
        <strong>Your collection</strong> of saved icons is stored in your browser (local storage).
        It never leaves your device unless you choose to share it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Recent searches</strong> shown in the search suggestions are stored the same way.
        Clearing your browser's site data removes both.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">What our servers keep</h2>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
      <li>
        <strong>Download counts:</strong> we count downloads only as totals per icon. Nothing about
        who downloaded is kept.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Shared collections:</strong> when you create a share link, we store the list of
        icons and the optional name you give it, so the link keeps working. Anyone with the link can
        see it. There is nothing personal in it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Logs:</strong> each request is logged with its method, path, status and timing,
        without IP addresses, user agents or query strings.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Abuse protection:</strong> to stop overload, we count requests per visitor using a
        one-way hash of the IP address. These counters expire within a minute.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">Hosting</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      Like most websites, IconNook is delivered through a content delivery network, which processes
      requests (including IP addresses) to serve and protect the site. We don't sell or share data
      with anyone else, and we don't use third-party analytics or ads.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">Questions</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      IconNook is open source, so you can read exactly what it does in the{' '}
      <a class="link" href={REPO}>
        source code
      </a>
      . For questions,{' '}
      <a class="link" href={`${REPO}/issues`}>
        open an issue
      </a>{' '}
      on GitHub.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
